# Dashboard (Next.js)

Developer-facing console: **memory explorer** (the demo money-shot), usage/cost analytics, API-key + billing management.

## Rules
- App Router + Server Components by default; client components only where interactivity is needed.
- Auth via BetterAuth; gate every page/route by tenant. Never render another tenant's data.
- The memory explorer must show, per memory: `content`, `type`, `score`, **provenance**, and a one-click delete (calls `DELETE /v1/memories/:id`).
- Reflect live updates via the SDK's pub/sub subscription so the explorer stays in sync.
- Surface usage vs. budget clearly (it ties to the rate limiter / cost story).

## UI
- Clean, modern, dense-but-readable infra-console aesthetic (think Clerk/Pinecone dashboards).
- Reuse shared types from `packages/core`; never re-fetch raw secrets to the client.
